Which build is this? It says so before the name
================================================

Two packages from one source tree, and once both are installed nothing on screen said
which one you were looking at. The name now carries a label in front of it — parentheses,
bold — in the three places a person actually looks: window title, sidebar brand, and the
tab title.

It is not hardcoded, because the label is the difference between the builds. It is read
from `QUIXI_EDITION_LABEL` when the package compiles:

    stock / core   (unset — the title is "QuixiDesk", byte for byte as upstream)
    personal       export QUIXI_EDITION_LABEL="(PERSONAL — volkdude85) "

so one patch serves every edition, and a build that sets nothing is unchanged. The shell
is static HTML served from disk, so the value is injected when the page is served instead
of being baked into each build's copy of the file.

Measured: a compile with the variable unset prints "QuixiDesk" and injects an empty
label; the same source compiled with it set prints "(PERSONAL — volkdude85) QuixiDesk".

--- a/crates/quixi-app/src/main.rs
+++ b/crates/quixi-app/src/main.rs
@@ -702,7 +702,17 @@
     // 5. SPA fallback -> ui/index.html for all client routes (/new, /chat/*, /cowork*, /code*, /settings*, etc.)
     let index_html = ui_dir.join("index.html");
     match fs::read(&index_html) {
-        Ok(bytes) => build_http_response(200, "text/html; charset=utf-8", bytes),
+        Ok(bytes) => {
+            // Tell the shell which build it is, so the brand line can carry the same label
+            // as the title bar. Injected at serve time because the HTML on disk is identical
+            // in every build — the label is the one thing that is not in the file.
+            let bootstrap = format!(
+                "<script>window.__QUIXI_EDITION__={label:?};</script>\n</head>",
+                label = EDITION_LABEL,
+            );
+            let html = String::from_utf8_lossy(&bytes).replacen("</head>", &bootstrap, 1);
+            build_http_response(200, "text/html; charset=utf-8", html.into_bytes())
+        }
         Err(err) => build_http_response(
             500,
             "text/plain; charset=utf-8",
@@ -711,6 +721,14 @@
     }
 }
 
+/// Which build this is. The packaging sets QUIXI_EDITION_LABEL when it compiles, so a
+/// single source tree produces every edition: a build that identifies itself says so in
+/// the title bar, and a stock build keeps upstream's name with no prefix at all.
+const EDITION_LABEL: &str = match option_env!("QUIXI_EDITION_LABEL") {
+    Some(label) => label,
+    None => "",
+};
